================================================================================
Title: Core-Collapse Supernovae from 9 to 120 Solar Masses Based 
       on Neutrino-powered Explosions  
Authors: Sukhbold T., Ertl T., Woosley S.E., Brown J.M., Janka H. 
================================================================================
Description of contents: progenitor_models/ (167Mb)
  these are 200 progenitor models from 9 to 120 solar masses. Note that the 
  mass increments are variable. Different pieces are taken directly or based 
  on the models from previous studies:
      9-13      = based on Woosley & Heger (2015)    [arXiv:1505.06712]
      13.1-14.9 = based on Sukhbold & Woosley (2014) [arXiv:1311.6546]
      15-30     = from     Sukhbold & Woosley (2014) [arXiv:1311.6546]
      >30       = from     Woosley & Heger (2007)    [arXiv:astro-ph/0702176]
  All models are calculated by the KEPLER code. Across different studies 
  obviously the code changes, but we assure that the changes are minimal for 
  the above. In the paper we have presented several 'extra' models to 
  demonstrate the agreement, especially between WH15 and SW14 models 
  (Section 2). Those are not provided here, but feel free to request them if 
  you're interested. 

System requirements: All files are ASCII tables.

Additional comments: Please get in touch with us if you're interested in 
the full zonal information from the big network - i.e. thousands of isotopes 
per each zone. 

================================================================================
